---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = "Splitting Rent & Groceries — Roommate";
const description = "Master bedroom vs small room? Who pays for shared oil vs personal snacks? Practical formulas and rules to split flat rent and groceries without disputes.";
const keywords = "how to split rent fairly, split groceries roommates, roommate utility split rules, fair bill splitting flatmates";

const articleSchema = {
  headline: title,
  description: description,
  datePublished: "2026-11-12T08:00:00Z",
  authorName: "Umesh Jaiswal"
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  keywords={keywords}
  ogType="article"
  publishDate="2026-11-12T08:00:00Z"
  articleSchema={articleSchema}
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: "Home", url: "https://roommatesexpensemanager.com" },
    { name: "Blog", url: "https://roommatesexpensemanager.com/blog" },
    { name: "Fair Split Formulas", url: "https://roommatesexpensemanager.com/blog/how-to-split-rent-and-groceries-equitably" }
  ]}
>
  <article class="max-w-[760px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-16 space-y-10 text-[#1d1d1f] dark:text-[#f5f5f7] text-[16px] sm:text-[17px] leading-relaxed transition-colors duration-200">
    <header class="space-y-4 border-b border-black/8 dark:border-white/10 pb-8">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-[#86868b] font-medium">
        <span class="px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-[#00966d]/10 dark:bg-[#00e599]/15 text-[#00966d] dark:text-[#00e599] font-semibold">Flatmate Etiquette</span>
        <span>•</span>
        <span>November 12, 2026</span>
        <span>•</span>
        <span>6 min read</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="apple-hero-display text-[#1d1d1f] dark:text-white tracking-tight leading-tight">
        How to Split Rent, Groceries, and Utilities Fairly (Formulas That Work)
      </h1>
      <p class="text-[18px] text-[#86868b] dark:text-[#a1a1a6] leading-relaxed">
        Disagreements about room sizes, air conditioning use, and who consumed the last egg ruin more friendships than major life conflicts. Here are proven formulas to keep things 100% fair.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="apple-display-lg text-[#1d1d1f] dark:text-white">1. Rent: Square Footage vs Equal Split</h2>
      <p class="text-[#1d1d1f]/90 dark:text-[#f5f5f7]/90 leading-relaxed">
        If one bedroom is a 200 sq.ft master bedroom with an attached balcony and private bath, and the other is a 110 sq.ft room with a shared hallway bathroom, splitting rent 50/50 is unfair and breeds resentment.
      </p>
      <div class="p-6 rounded-[22px] bg-[#f5f5f7] dark:bg-[#1d1d1f] border border-black/8 dark:border-white/10 space-y-2">
        <p class="font-bold text-[#00966d] dark:text-[#00e599] text-[15px]">The 50/50 Common Area Formula:</p>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-[14px] text-[#86868b] dark:text-[#a1a1a6] leading-relaxed">
          Allocate <strong>50% of the rent</strong> equally to all roommates for shared spaces (living room, kitchen, balcony, amenities). Allocate the remaining <strong>50% of the rent</strong> strictly proportionally based on private bedroom square footage and private bathroom perks.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="apple-display-lg text-[#1d1d1f] dark:text-white">2. Groceries: The "Shared vs Solo" Rule</h2>
      <p class="text-[#1d1d1f]/90 dark:text-[#f5f5f7]/90 leading-relaxed">
        The golden rule for shared kitchen supplies:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 text-[#86868b] dark:text-[#a1a1a6] pl-2 text-[15px]">
        <li><strong>Shared:</strong> Cooking oil, salt, spices, dishwashing soap, trash bags, drinking water cans, milk for tea. Split equally among all flatmates in Roommate.</li>
        <li><strong>Solo:</strong> Expensive meats, specialty cheeses, premium snacks, protein powder, or alcohol. Kept private; whoever buys it pays 100% for it.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="apple-display-lg text-[#1d1d1f] dark:text-white">3. High Utility Spikes (AC & Heaters)</h2>
      <p class="text-[#1d1d1f]/90 dark:text-[#f5f5f7]/90 leading-relaxed">
        If one roommate runs a 1.5-ton AC for 14 hours a day during hot summer months while others rely on ceiling fans, splitting the electricity bill equally causes fights.
      </p>
      <p class="text-[#1d1d1f]/90 dark:text-[#f5f5f7]/90 leading-relaxed">
        Calculate the baseline winter electricity bill (e.g. ₹800). Any summer spike above that baseline (e.g. bill is ₹3,800, so a ₹3,000 spike) should have 70% paid by the AC user and 30% split across the flat.
      </p>
    </section>

    <footer class="pt-8 border-t border-black/8 dark:border-white/10 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4">
      <div>
        <p class="text-[17px] font-semibold text-[#1d1d1f] dark:text-white">Log your fair splits in seconds.</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-[#86868b]">Free forever, zero caps, and instant PIN login.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
        <a href="http://localhost:5173" class="apple-btn-primary">
          Open Roommate App
        </a>
        <a href="/blog" class="apple-btn-secondary">
          <span>All Guides</span>
          <span aria-hidden="true">›</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
